        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>To document tenderness elicited by palpation during physical examination.</purpose>
      <keywords>Tenderness, elicited pain, palpation, physical exam.</keywords>
      <use>To record the presence and summary characteristics of tenderness elicited on palpation.&#xD;
&#xD;
This archetype has been specifically designed to be used within CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. &#xD;
&#xD;
Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element.</use>
      <misuse>Not to be used for recording the clinical history - use specific OBSERVATION and CLUSTER archetypes. For example OBSERVATION.story and CLUSTER.symptom_sign.&#xD;
&#xD;
Not to be used for recording the results of an imaging examination - use the CLUSTER.imaging_exam family of archetypes for this purpose.</misuse>
